; NextDAAD SP18 item 7 Task 7 fixture - the dual-channel SD-streamed
; sampled-effect wire smoke.
;
; Compiled by tests\build-tests.ps1 on every run (a break in the DSF is
; caught even without the leg switch, same rule the other fixtures
; follow); staged as the active GAME.DDB in sd\SFXLONG\ by
; tests\build-tests.ps1 -SfxLong, which also generates and stages the
; two stimulus WAVs described below as 001.WAV and 002.WAV. sd\SFXLONG\
; is emptied and refilled on every -SfxLong run and holds nothing but
; those two files plus a NEXTDAAD.NEX copy of build\nextdaad.nex - copy
; the folder to the card and launch from inside it.
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHY THIS FIXTURE EXISTS
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; Tasks 5-6 landed the SD-streamed sampled-effect machinery
; (src\audio\streamfx.asm): a WAV whose file size is <= SFX_WIN_BYTES
; (24576 bytes, src\nextdaad.inc) stages whole and plays COMPLETE - the
; original free-hybrid, fully resident path; a larger WAV stages its
; first SFX_WIN_BYTES and the per-tick refiller (aud_sfx_refill) tops
; the window up with raw CMD18 SD reads while it plays - STREAMING.
; Nothing in the automated harness had reached the STREAMING arm before
; this task: every WAV staged by every other leg (-SfxDi's 48044-byte
; tones included) happens to exceed the same threshold too, but nothing
; asserted which arm actually ran or watched the refiller's own
; counters. This fixture puts one WAV of each size on the card, with
; verbs to trigger every SFX sub the machinery ships, so the staged
; bytes and the compiled condacts are asserted here even though the
; refiller itself can only be watched on real SD hardware (see the
; ZEsarUX section below).
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; THE TWO EFFECTS
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; Effect 1 (001.WAV) - THE STREAMER. ~200000 bytes of payload (200044
; bytes on disk with the 44-byte RIFF/fmt/data header), 16000 Hz mono
; 8-bit unsigned - comfortably over SFX_WIN_BYTES, so sfx_stream_open
; takes the STREAMING arm and the refiller has to keep feeding it for
; the whole ~12.5 s runtime.
;
; Effect 2 (002.WAV) - THE COMPLETE FILE. ~16000 bytes of payload
; (16044 bytes on disk), same rate/format - comfortably under
; SFX_WIN_BYTES, so sfx_stream_open takes the free-hybrid COMPLETE arm
; and nothing streams: the refiller owes this channel no blocks at all.
; Its only job here is proving that a same-format, same-leg small file
; keeps working exactly as it always did while the other channel is
; mid-stream.
;
; Both files are generated inline in tests\build-tests.ps1's -SfxLong
; staging block (a 20-line PowerShell RIFF/fmt/data writer, the same
; idiom the truncwav/badwav suite fixtures already use elsewhere in
; that script) - deterministic whole-cycle 8-bit sine payloads centred
; on 128 (DAC_SILENCE), same construction as tests\audio\mktone.py's
; tones, so re-running the stager reproduces the exact same bytes.
; Nothing here is a copy of a Python-generated file: the brief called
; for an inline generator specifically because these two sizes are not
; shared with any other fixture's tone.
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; THE VERBS
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; SFX B C: B = effect number, C = sub. Only subs 1 (play once), 2 (play
; looped) and 5 (stop all channels) are shipped - subs 11-16 do not
; exist yet and must not be used here.
;   PLAY1  SFX 1 1   effect 1 (the streamer) once
;   LOOP1  SFX 1 2   effect 1 (the streamer) looped
;   PLAY2  SFX 2 1   effect 2 (the complete file) once
;   LOOP2  SFX 2 2   effect 2 (the complete file) looped
;   STOP   SFX 0 5   stop every playing channel (both effects)
; Boot autoplay triggers LOOP1 automatically (see /PRO 6) so the
; ZEsarUX smoke below needs no typing at all past launching the .nex -
; the verbs exist for exercising the other subs and effect 2 by hand.
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; THE DDB BYTE-ASSERT (the fixture-stimulus rule)
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; DRC silently rewrites some condacts (BEEP tone range, PAUSE duration
; scaling - see tests\audlad.dsf and tests\sfxdi.dsf's own headers), so
; what the interpreter actually receives is verified against the
; compiled bytes, not assumed from this source. tests\build-tests.ps1
; dumps tests\out\sfxlong.ddb and asserts SFX 1 1, SFX 1 2, SFX 2 1,
; SFX 2 2 and SFX 0 5 (opcode 18 = $12) are all present as authored,
; the same idiom the sfxdi/fontsw blocks already use.
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; ZESARUX MANUAL WIRE SMOKE (owner procedure - not automated)
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; CSpect has no raw SPI, so it cannot exercise the refiller's CMD18
; path at all - only real SD hardware or ZEsarUX's SD emulation can.
; ZEsarUX's raw SD SPI streaming (port $EB, CMD18) is hardware-proven
; to work; its CTC hw-IM2 audio path is frozen
; (does not advance), so this smoke proves the WIRE AND BOOKKEEPING -
; staged bytes, depth accounting, no hang - not audio quality. Audio
; verdicts are Task 14's silicon legs.
;
; Procedure:
;   1. Build a DEBUG interpreter (.\build.ps1, no -Release/-Kit - the
;      default build already defines DDEBUG=1) and stage this leg
;      (.\tests\build-tests.ps1 -SfxLong).
;   2. Mount sd\SFXLONG\ as the SD card in ZEsarUX (or copy it to a
;      real card and mount that).
;   3. Run NEXTDAAD.NEX from inside that folder.
;   4. Boot autoplay triggers LOOP1 (the streamer) with no typing
;      needed; let it run 60 s.
;   5. Read the DEBUG SFX= row (row 31, column 56 on screen - printed
;      by sfx_dbg_row, src\audio\streamfx.asm): it reads
;      "SFX=<refilled hex16>/<underrun hex16>/<fails hex8>". Pass
;      criteria: refilled blocks > 0 (the refiller actually ran),
;      underruns = 0, fails = 0.
;   6. Quit. Any fail here is a logic bug in the wire/bookkeeping - fix
;      before silicon, do not wait for Task 14.
; Scripted ZEsarUX automation of this procedure is out of scope for
; this task.
;
; CSpect expectation (for whoever runs this leg there instead, or by
; mistake): effect 2 (COMPLETE, no streaming) plays exactly as every
; other sampled effect in this project always has. Effect 1 stages its
; first SFX_WIN_BYTES normally (that part is an ordinary sequential
; file read, not raw SPI) and then the refiller's raw-SPI CMD18 polls
; find nothing behind CSpect's SD emulation and fail - bounded by
; SFX_FAIL_LIMIT (src\audio\streamfx.asm, 8 consecutive failed ticks,
; or immediately if the very first block after the stage never
; delivered), so the channel stops cleanly rather than hanging or
; crashing. This is expected CSpect behaviour, not a defect - see the
; refiller's own CSpect-degradation analysis for the tick-cost
; arithmetic.
;
; EAR EXPECTATION (for the runsheet this leg's header text feeds -
; Task 14): a >24K LOOPING effect has an audible seam at the loop
; point on real hardware - a brief DC HOLD (the refiller's last
; delivered sample held one extra period while the window empties and
; refills), NOT a silent gap. Do not mistake the hold for a dropout.

; System flags used by name (DAAD BLANK template spellings)
#define fPlayer             38
#define fDarkF              28

/CTL
_
/VOC
NORTH  2  noun
SOUTH  3  noun
LOOK   4  verb
PLAY1  60 verb
LOOP1  61 verb
PLAY2  62 verb
LOOP2  63 verb
STOP   64 verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key."
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "NEXTDAAD SD-STREAMED SFX FIXTURE (SP18 ITEM 7 TASK 7)#n"
/OTX
/0 "a brass lamp"
/LTX
/0 ""
/1 "The listening room."
/CON
/0
NORTH 1
/1
SOUTH 0
/OBJ
/0    1   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
> _ _   AT 0
        PROCESS 6
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 25 127
        CLEAR fDarkF
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        DESC @fPlayer
> _ _   PROCESS 1
/PRO 1
> _ _   PARSE 0
        REDO
> _ _   PROCESS 5
        ISDONE
        REDO
> _ _   MOVE fPlayer
        CLS
        RESTART
> _ _   SYSMESS 8
        REDO
/PRO 5
; ---- effect 1, 001.WAV, the streamer (> SFX_WIN_BYTES) ----
> PLAY1 _ MES "effect 1 (streamer) once - SFX 1 1#n"
          SFX 1 1
          DONE
> LOOP1 _ MES "effect 1 (streamer) looped - SFX 1 2#n"
          SFX 1 2
          DONE
; ---- effect 2, 002.WAV, the complete file (<= SFX_WIN_BYTES) ----
> PLAY2 _ MES "effect 2 (complete) once - SFX 2 1#n"
          SFX 2 1
          DONE
> LOOP2 _ MES "effect 2 (complete) looped - SFX 2 2#n"
          SFX 2 2
          DONE
; ---- stop everything ----
> STOP  _ MES "all channels stopped - SFX 0 5#n"
          SFX 0 5
          DONE
/PRO 6
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 25 127
        PAPER 0
        INK 7
        CLS
        MESSAGE 0
> _ _   MES "001.WAV effect 1, > 24K, STREAMING#n"
        MES "002.WAV effect 2, <= 24K, COMPLETE#n#n"
        MES "PLAY1 / LOOP1              effect 1 once / looped#n"
        MES "PLAY2 / LOOP2              effect 2 once / looped#n"
        MES "STOP                       stop every channel#n#n"
        MES "Boot autoplay starts LOOP1 automatically.#n"
; Boot autoplay - the ZEsarUX wire smoke needs no typed input at all:
; launch the .nex and read the DEBUG SFX= row after 60 s.
> _ _   SFX 1 2
        GOTO 1
/END
